1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,450
Ek Phone: an offline study app for several kids who share one phone.

2
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:08,950
The barrier: most study apps assume one child, one phone, an account and mobile data.

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:12,950
An empty phone. One tap on "Try the demo" loads 4 made-up learners.

4
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:17,450
Each child has a name tag. No email, no account. Zara's demo PIN is 1234.

5
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:22,950
Zara taps her name and types her 4-digit PIN.

6
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:27,450
Her own shelf opens. Today's lesson shows its size first: 4.2 KB.

7
00:00:27,500 --> 00:00:30,950
The yellow highlighter marks one sentence at a time.

8
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:38,450
The arrow keys (or the arrow buttons) move it sentence by sentence.

9
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:41,950
Then a 5-question quiz on the same lesson.

10
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:45,950
Every answer gets feedback. Right...

11
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:50,450
...or wrong, with the right answer and the reason.

12
00:00:50,500 --> 00:00:54,950
Zara got 4 of 5. The score is saved on this phone, for Zara only.

13
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:58,450
Her shelf moves on to the next lesson.

14
00:00:58,500 --> 00:01:02,450
On the name screen, a tick shows who has studied today.

15
00:01:02,500 --> 00:01:06,950
Hamza's shelf is his own. His lesson is still "Not started".

16
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:11,450
One tap switches the whole app to Urdu: right to left, Nastaliq script.

17
00:01:11,500 --> 00:01:15,950
In Urdu the arrow keys follow the reading direction.

18
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:19,450
A teacher or older sibling opens "Lesson packs" and "Write a lesson".

19
00:01:19,500 --> 00:01:22,950
Open a .txt, .md or .pdf file, or paste the text.

20
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:27,450
A .txt file comes in: 6 sentences and 5 suggested questions.

21
00:01:27,500 --> 00:01:30,950
The first line becomes the title. The rest is split into sentences.

22
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:34,950
Suggested questions are fill-in-the-blank, with the right answer marked.

23
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:40,950
The teacher checks each one and edits it before saving.

24
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:44,950
The preview shows the size: 1.2 KB, 6 sentences, 5 questions.

25
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:48,450
Saved. Every learner on this phone now sees it.

26
00:01:48,500 --> 00:01:51,950
The new lesson is in the pack list, marked "Written here".

27
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:55,950
"Show QR codes": this lesson needs 3 codes.

28
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:00,450
Each code is a link into the app, so any phone camera can open it.

29
00:02:00,500 --> 00:02:03,450
The codes cycle by themselves. Sharing uses 0 MB of mobile data.

30
00:02:03,500 --> 00:02:07,950
A second browser, standing in for phone B, opens the links: "Got 1 of 3".

31
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:12,450
After all 3, it shows the size before loading: 1.2 KB.

32
00:02:12,500 --> 00:02:15,950
Loaded. The lesson is now on every learner's shelf on phone B.

33
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:20,450
Back on phone A: network off (browser offline mode), page reloaded.

34
00:02:20,500 --> 00:02:24,950
It still opens from the service worker, and the lesson still reads.

35
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:29,450
Built during AccessED Hacks (Oct 17 to Nov 20, 2026) by Muhammad Faizan.

36
00:02:29,500 --> 00:02:33,950
Not yet tested: real read-aloud voices, TalkBack, and two physical cameras.

37
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:38,450
Try it at ekphone-app.vercel.app. Code: github.com/MuhammadFaizan-prog/ekphone

